{
  "_comment": [
    "The order pipeline `setup-demo.sh` seeds, as records rather than as digests.",
    "",
    "Records and not digests, deliberately: a digest is what this application computes, so",
    "committing one would let the fixture and the digester drift together and agree with each",
    "other about a payload neither had read. These are the payloads the seeder writes, verbatim,",
    "and the eval digests them with the real PayloadDigestService.",
    "",
    "`baseTimestampMs` plus each record's `atMs` fixes the broker clock, which is the clock that",
    "matters here: the seeder stamps every step of one order with the *same* `event_time`, so a",
    "mapped business timestamp would tie across all six hops. On this dataset the hop timing is",
    "the broker's, DEMO_HOP_DELAY is what produces it, and the offsets below reproduce its shape",
    "(the 3 -> 4 hop is 3x the others, per STEP_PAUSE).",
    "",
    "`docs/check-eval-fixture.py` resolves every topic and key claimed here against setup-demo.sh,",
    "so this file cannot quietly describe a dataset the seeder no longer produces."
  ],
